text:
maria: FYI i'm landing a docs update for aurora-x / aurora-lite variants - needs migration snippets (sdk v3->v4), compatibility note, and small benchmark addendum. PR: https://github.com/redwood/inference-docs/pull/4399
kevin: I'll sync the model-catalog CSV after we pick the final max_sequence_length values. Do we have final ceilings per variant?
maria: Runtime gave preliminary ceilings: aurora-x (fp16) 8192, aurora-x-quant 6144, aurora-lite3b 4096. We'll label them "hardware-dependent" and point to the catalog for exact per-variant numbers.
ashley: I'll add two snippets: 1) SDK v4 resolve+generate with fallback for quantized variants, 2) embeddings example that shows model.resolveVariant usage. Keep them minimal so they fit side-by-side in the model card.
samir: Quick product ask 1 1 can we pause public deprecation for aurora-lite3b until ops confirms no pinned reservations? We had a customer last week with an explicit pin.
maria: Good catch. We'll mark the card with a scheduled deprecation banner but don't flip it until ops gives the greenlight. I'll add the banner behind a feature flag in the PR.
jen: tiny nit: replace `sequence_length_limit` with `max_sequence_length` in all examples (we normalized this key last release). Also remove stray trailing comma in the JSON examples.
kevin: For benchmarks, let's add one row comparing q4_0 vs fp16 at bsz=1/8/32 and add a short footnote "results vary by GPU family and kernel selection". I'll create a follow-up PR to update the generated table from CSV -> docs.
ashley: paste sdk snippet i'm adding for review:
```js
// SDK v4: prefer quantized, fall back to compat alias
const variant = await client.models.resolveVariant('aurora-x', { preferQuantized: true });
try {
  const res = await client.generate({ model: variant, input: prompt });
  console.log(res.generated_text);
} catch (err) {
  // fallback to compat variant alias
  const fallback = 'aurora-x-compat-q4_0';
  const res2 = await client.generate({ model: fallback, input: prompt });
  console.log(res2.generated_text);
}
```
maria: looks good. can you also add the curl example for folks on the CLI: `curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -d '{"model":"aurora-x:compat-q4_0","input":"..."}'`
ashley: adding that now. also included an embeddings snippet showing `client.embed({model: variant, input: text})` and note about shard count for large corpora.
samir: prod-ops responded: safe to publish docs but hold the banner flip until friday EOD to give customers time to change pinned configs.
maria: i'll add a TODO in the PR and schedule the banner flip for friday. thanks. :thumbsup:
docs-bot: preview deployed: https://deploy-preview.redwood-docs.io/pr-4399  (CI #11402 passed) :white_check_mark:
kevin: one more: update model card example key `max_sequence_length` in the YAML frontmatter and regenerate the HTML table. I'll link the follow-up CSV PR in the doc footnote.
maria: will do. merging plan: small edits now, wait for ops greenlight, then merge and flip the banner friday. if any blockers surface i'll ping here.
jen: LGTM for the JSON key change.
ashley: updated snippets and CLI alias. pushed changes to the PR branch.
samir: i'll monitor ops and report back if anything changes.
maria: thanks all, closing loop tomorrow morning when ops confirms.
